Revision history for ansi2pdf

0.1.5 2026-11-11T09:23:38Z

    - A kanji with an ideographic variation selector (U+E0100 to
      U+E01EF) is no longer reported as "no font has"; it was drawn
      correctly, and only the message was wrong

0.1.4 2026-11-11T04:25:48Z

    - The margin can be given with the paper name after ":m", the
      same as -m: "-p a4p:m10" is A4 in portrait with a margin of
      10 mm, and "-p a4:m0" is A4 without a margin; the last of -m
      and such a paper name is used
    - The default margin is 5 mm; it was 10 mm, which is for printing
      and binding, and is too wide to read the PDF on a screen.  The
      same options now give a slightly larger font and fewer columns;
      give -m 10 for the margin of the earlier versions

0.1.3 2026-11-11T03:00:20Z

    - The orientation can be given with the paper name: "-p a4p" is
      A4 in portrait and "-p a4l" is A4 in landscape, the same as
      "-p a4 -P" and "-p a4 -L"; a hyphen may be put before the
      letter, as "-p letter-l"
    - It counts with -L and -P, the last of which decides the
      orientation; a name without the letter leaves the orientation
      as it was

0.1.2 2026-11-10T13:14:14Z

    - The lines (-l), the columns (-w) and the font size (-s) follow
      each other: the ones that are given are kept, and the others
      are decided to fill the page
    - The default of 60 lines is used only when none of them is
      given; it was always used, so that -w left a part of the page
      blank, and -s with a large font put 60 lines beyond the page

0.1.1 2026-11-10T12:55:17Z

    - Separate the columns and the rows of -C with a comma, as
      "-C 2,2"; "-C 2.2" of 0.1.0 is no longer accepted

0.1.0 2026-11-10T11:44:33Z

    - First version, which renders terminal output with ANSI
      sequences to PDF
    - Colors, bold, faint, italic, underlines of every style and
      color, reverse video, strikethrough and overline are kept; box
      drawing characters and block elements are drawn as lines and
      rectangles
    - The input is interpreted by xterm.js, so cursor movement,
      background fill, wide characters and line wrapping come out as
      on a terminal; a form feed and clearing the screen start a new
      page
    - Logical pages are arranged on a sheet with -C, with a border
      (-B) and a header (-H)
    - Characters missing in the main font are drawn with fallback
      fonts; without BIZ UDGothic, Menlo or DejaVu Sans Mono is used
    - --geometry tells the size of a logical page to a program that
      formats text for it
